{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1083939-effects-of-xenomorph-impregnation-oh-various-splats","id":1083939,"title":"Effects of Xenomorph impregnation oh various splats.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-26T06:32:04-07:00","id":1083939,"title":"Effects of Xenomorph impregnation oh various splats.","content":"So... Alien: Covenant is going to be going out soon and a poster I saw made me wonder about how it would work with... less than human creatures since Xenomorph canonically have changes based on their host.<br /> <br /> <br /> So some questions.<br /> Assuming that a face hugger somehow managed to impregnate a supernatural, how badly would the... birth affect it? What means of getting rid of are available to a supernatural? What complications are probably going to arrise due to the strange nature of some supernatural beings and their powers? (All of the undead ones have certain.... quucks i wager) How fucked would things be if a supernatural chest burster gains a significant portion of the oddities that it's &quot;parent&quot; had?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T07:10:50-07:00","id":1083953,"title":"","content":"Werewolf ones would be... <i>bad</i>. Vampire and Mummy ones might not even be able to mature, the hosts being dead and all. For Demons, they'd probably count as Offspring. Mages' likely wouldn't have that much different, since Mages are physically human and their power come from enlightenment (which I doubt is transferable).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T08:46:40-07:00","id":1083990,"title":"","content":"Notably, the side effects of being...facehugged?... include ravenous hunger. That's going to be really bad for vampires and werewolves, may send a promethean into instant torment based on the rules and, if it applies to Hunger as well as hunger, beasts would become <i>terrifying</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T10:49:54-07:00","id":1084058,"title":"","content":"I think that's supposed to be the host getting driven to fuel the growth of the xenomorph growing inside them. It would make no sense to apply that to spiritual hungers. I'm not sure vampires could even support one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T11:12:33-07:00","id":1084070,"title":"","content":"Vampires are dead but the tissue is not broken down, so it depends on whether or not the chestburster requires body heat while developing. Then there's also the Cleansing during daysleep which might eject the growing xenomorph.<br /> <br /> I'm going to be boring but unless the xenomorph has any way of picking up supernatural abilities then neither of the splats would be able to grant it abilities beyond a normal mortal <i>unless </i>the host changes shape. Werewolves, vampires with Protean 3 and people subject to certain Life spells could possibly impart different characteristics depending on their shape during the &quot;incubation period&quot;.<br /> A Gauru based xenomorph would be terrifying, but highly unlikely considering the increased regeneration while in Gauru.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T11:45:37-07:00","id":1084084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1083939-effects-of-xenomorph-impregnation-oh-various-splats?p=1084058#post1084058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that's supposed to be the host getting driven to fuel the growth of the xenomorph growing inside them. It would make no sense to apply that to spiritual hungers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean on the one hand true but on the other hand when else to you get to say &quot;turns out it wasn't a ravenous beast, it was actually a xenomorph from space! Your dreams are attacked by facehuggers.&quot; in your game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T15:27:46-07:00","id":1084185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1083939-effects-of-xenomorph-impregnation-oh-various-splats?p=1083953#post1083953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolf ones would be... <i>bad</i>. Vampire and Mummy ones might not even be able to mature, the hosts being dead and all. For Demons, they'd probably count as Offspring. Mages' likely wouldn't have that much different, since Mages are physically human and their power come from enlightenment (which I doubt is transferable).</div> </div> </div> </div>This is pretty much my assessment as well.<br /> Vampires, mummies, and prometheans would probably not be viable hosts.<br /> <br /> Mages, changelings, and bound would produce regular human-incubated xenomorphs.<br /> <br /> Demons would produce Offspring xenomorphs, which is a pretty scary thought.<br /> <br /> Werewolves would produce shapeshifting, regenerating xenomorphs, which is absolutely terrifying.<br /> <br /> I don't know enough about Beasts to say what the result there would be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T15:45:11-07:00","id":1084191,"title":"","content":"As for Beasts:<br /> <br /> Were they facehugged in the mortal realm, where they're basically human? That'd be normal xenomorphs.<br /> <br /> Were they facehugged in their Lairs, where they've merged with their Horrors? Now <i>that</i> is a horrifying idea. You'd have huge, hulking xenomorphs with the ability to feed psychically off of fear, and probably will gain a Lair, much later on in life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T15:51:20-07:00","id":1084193,"title":"","content":"I doubt that werewolves would pass on their &quot;physical&quot; powers since they're part of their half-ephemeral nature. Just like I wouldn't expect vampires to be able to pass on the physical disciplines should they be viable hosts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T16:13:21-07:00","id":1084197,"title":"","content":"I mean, given how integral the half-spiritness is to werewolves I could see them making half-spirit xenomorphs. Aliens but now they can take on human form and travel through the shadow.<br /> <br /> They should at least make wolf-blooded xenomophs which,depending on the tell, could be terrifying enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12109,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","user":"Urbenmyth","date":". 04-26-2017, 07:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T18:55:38-07:00","id":1084241,"title":"","content":"I, for one, would dread running into a xenomorph that popped out of a Deviant...<br /> <br /> Also, I'd go the other way around - xenomorphs that pop out of a werewolf are based off whatever form they were in at the time (it integrates itself into your system, you see). No, the problem is that the chestburster doesn't <i>kill</i> the werewolf. So theoretically, you could have a single werewolf become a chestburster <i>factory</i>...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T22:48:24-07:00","id":1084349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1083939-effects-of-xenomorph-impregnation-oh-various-splats?p=1084193#post1084193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I doubt that werewolves would pass on their &amp;quot;physical&amp;quot; powers since they're part of their half-ephemeral nature. Just like I wouldn't expect vampires to be able to pass on the physical disciplines should they be viable hosts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. Given how strong 2e drives home the &quot;werewolves are not human and never were&quot; vibe, I feel like shapeshifting and regeneration and the like are as much bilological traits as they are metaphysical. We see from Sundered World as well that werewolves aren't really half-spirit, so much as they're all-pangaean, which are similar to spirits but are indeed made of matter instead of ephemera.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T23:02:24-07:00","id":1084352,"title":"","content":"The nanutari always reminded me, visually, of xenomorphs.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Sf6WAAX.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> But yeah, werewolves wouldn't have 'wolf' xenomorphs they'd more likely have some sort of weird spirit-hybrid. But you would likely be able to do some sort of crude surgery to remove the chestburster before it burst. Or they could try going gauru during the stage when it's trying to come out to just survive it. They do deal with similar things, like the beshilu who are known to dig into peoples bellies, eat and replace their heart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T00:53:15-07:00","id":1084375,"title":"","content":"Would vampires produce ghouled xenomorphs? Given blood bonds there is a certain appeal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12243-dreaming-cat","name":"Dreaming Cat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T01:26:11-07:00","id":1084382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1083939-effects-of-xenomorph-impregnation-oh-various-splats?p=1084191#post1084191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Beasts:<br /> <br /> Were they facehugged in the mortal realm, where they're basically human? That'd be normal xenomorphs.<br /> <br /> Were they facehugged in their Lairs, where they've merged with their Horrors? Now <i>that</i> is a horrifying idea. You'd have huge, hulking xenomorphs with the ability to feed psychically off of fear, and probably will gain a Lair, much later on in life.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering Beasts are the physical encarnation of a Nightmare, a Xenomorph born from one in his Horror form would be...<br /> ...I, I think I will go to bed with the lights on this night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T05:37:05-07:00","id":1084424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1083939-effects-of-xenomorph-impregnation-oh-various-splats?p=1084382#post1084382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Considering Beasts are the physical encarnation of a Nightmare, a Xenomorph born from one in his Horror form would be...<br /> ...I, I think I will go to bed with the lights on this night.</div> </div> </div> </div>Won't stop them","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T20:48:55-07:00","id":1084850,"title":"","content":"If you want your Xenos to overcome biological/magical limitations of gestation with supernaturals, say the eggs are the inert fragments of a heretofore unprecedented Idigam Host and watch the players burst into a cold sweat.<br /> <br /> Seriously, I feel like Father Wolf would've come away from that fight missing some swatches of hair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1289,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","user":"Hastur00","date":". 04-27-2017, 11:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T20:56:26-07:00","id":1084855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hastur00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1083939-effects-of-xenomorph-impregnation-oh-various-splats?p=1084850#post1084850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want your Xenos to overcome biological/magical limitations of gestation with supernaturals, say the eggs are the inert fragments of a heretofore unprecedented Idigam Host and watch the players burst into a cold sweat.<br /> <br /> Seriously, I feel like Father Wolf would've come away from that fight missing some swatches of hair.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love this idea. I might use something like this in a future Werewolf game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T21:33:43-07:00","id":1084873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1083939-effects-of-xenomorph-impregnation-oh-various-splats?p=1084855#post1084855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love this idea. I might use something like this in a future Werewolf game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Use it in good health. Give 'em hell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T02:36:57-07:00","id":1084936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1083939-effects-of-xenomorph-impregnation-oh-various-splats?p=1084855#post1084855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love this idea. I might use something like this in a future Werewolf game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well Alien Covenant happens really soon. So to get the ready force them to watch it before hand..<br /> <br /> <br /> We also have the option of just labeling the Alien as some weird precursor thing..... afterall Engineer are, despite their... well, limitations older than life on Earth","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T19:13:16-07:00","id":1085281,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I see no reason why Aliens wouldn't take on the physiological traits of supernaturals, even if it comes from more metaphysical differences. Vampires, even without factors like Blood Magic stuff, still have things like Physical Intensity, Disciplines like Celerity or Protean that are mostly physiological in nature, or things like Auspex that are mostly sensory.<br /> <br /> I can see things like Mage magic not transferring (unless we want to talk about Proximus Aliens*, ye gods!), but even some other traits like a Changeling Seemings (Ogres might produce bigger, bulkier Aliens, Fairest might birth eerily alluring monsters, etc.) could reasonably affect the resulting monster.<br /> <br /> *<sup>Yes, I know that it's more complicated than Proximus = Mage Baby, but it's a plausible source for at least one Proximus, and the idea is horrifying enough to be worth it.</sup><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T23:46:40-07:00","id":1085378,"title":"","content":"This of course assumes that the xenomorph isn't adjusted for the setting, like a seer bound horror from the abyss that steals supernal power, a form that strix can take on once they possess a powerful enough vampire, a horrifying product of pandoran alchemy, some beast's astral offspring from their lairs, an idigam, a rogue minion of the mummies from ancient Irem, a terrifying new kind of huntsman, some ancient horror of the underworld and of course a slasher with a variety of shapeshifting techniques","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T03:43:35-07:00","id":1085414,"title":"","content":"What a beautifully frightening idea!<br /> <br /> I agree with the general consensus here: Mummies, Kindred, and possibly Prometheans would probably not provide a suitable host.<br /> Demon-, Werewolf- and Beast-spawned Xenos would be utterly horrifying. About Beasts, I've always read the Atavisms as physical change, taking on properties of their Horror, so to speak, so at the very least they should 'pass on' such things as Cyclopean Strength.<br /> Depending on Circumstances, these three also have pretty good chances of surviving the whole Chestburster experience.<br /> And I agree with Charlaquin and malonkey1: certain supernatural abilities are so inbound into the template they should carry on, metaphysical origin or not.<br /> <br /> I think Changeling hosts would and should produce non-normal Xenos, after all, Changelings are very different from vanilla mortals, albeit I'd be unsure how Elemental Xenos would turn out.<br /> And speaking of mortals, this brings me to our Hunter-Templates: what would happen with a Lucifuge-spawned Xenomorph? After all, it's a demonic host.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T07:08:50-07:00","id":1085439,"title":"","content":"In the case of changelings, I'd say the incubation depends on how much of the Mien is still effectively made of flesh. Changelings with higher Wyrd tend to have more fantastical Miens, especially Elementals. They probably would not gain Contracts, but might gain the ability to harvest Glamour through fear and use it to enter and shape the Hedge. From that point onward, they could build special Hollow-like hives and use hobgoblins for incubation.<br /> <br /> In the case of the Lucifuge, I assume the xenomorph might gain Castigations that let it assume a demonic form and such, but not those that control fire or demons (since xenomorphs are afraid of fire and would not be seen as legitimate heirs).<br /> <br /> By the way, Reighnhell wrote <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show?p=1085446#post1085446\"><b>stats for the xenomorph.</b></a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 04-29-2017, 10:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T07:09:51-07:00","id":1085440,"title":"","content":"Would Changeling Chestbursters have a Mask?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T07:09:51-07:00","id":1085441,"title":"","content":"Double post","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T07:09:51-07:00","id":1085442,"title":"","content":"Triple post","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T07:35:07-07:00","id":1085450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1083939-effects-of-xenomorph-impregnation-oh-various-splats?p=1085440#post1085440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would Changeling Chestbursters have a Mask?</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if the Chestbursters and the Warriors had Masks, they wouldn't be very useful, since they can't act like humans. Instead, I assume their version of the Mask would make them even better at stealth instead of actually hiding their true form behind an illusion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T08:17:33-07:00","id":1085460,"title":"","content":"<b>Re: Xenomorph Hybrid</b><br /> <br /> I come in on the side that says that a Xenomorph is a strictly biological creature, as such would not be able to interface with any supernatural trait that isn't also strictly biological. A xenomorph should be able to impregnate a Vampire anymore than it could impregnate an Android. <br /> <br /> But that isn't any fun! So lets assume that the xenomorph physiology and absorb some degree of otherworldly traits.<br /> <br /> <b>Vampire:</b> A Vampire is a Walking Corpse, so it wouldn't an appealing target to a Protomorph (aka Facehugger) in most situation. However, a Vampire using Blush of Life would register as alive enough to be attacked. Once implanted,the creature would grow from the Vampires vitae, creating a Xenomorphic Ghoul - with all the powers and abilities a ghoul would normally have. Luckily a Vampire would likely be able to cut the creature out of its body while gestating, and would be able to survive the chestburster experience.<br /> <br /> <b>Werewolf:</b> A werewolf would be a prime target for the Protomorph. Luckily, a Werewolves healing would treat the embryo like any other foreign parasite, and would quickly try to destroy it (a Werewolf with Primal Urge 3+ would likely be completely immune) . However, assuming the Xenomorph comes to term, it would posses a Werewolves regeneration, and its ability to cross between worlds, with the drive and ability to prey on ephemeral as well as physical creatures. It would also gain a Werewolves vulnerability to Silver. Werewolves are supernaturally hardy, and can survive a chestburster, probably recovering in enough time to hunt down the larval Xenomorph.<br /> <br /> <b>Mage: </b>Despite the immense power a Mage commands, they are fundamentally human in a way most other supernaturals are not. As such, they would endure the implantation process as well as any other human (ie. not well at all). The resultant Xenomorph would be a typical specimen, but might be drawn to magical phenomena and become a stalker of Mages. A Mage would be able to clear the infection with proper magical treatment.<br /> <br /> <b>Changelings:</b> Changelings exhibit such variation that it would be hard to predict what would happen. Some might be ignored by protomorphs, or hardy enough to resist infection. Others would be effectively human and produce relatively typical Xenomorphs. The most likely thing a Xenomorph would gain is an attunement to the Wyrd, allow it to identify changelings and to cross into the Hedge while stalking prey.<br /> <br /> <b>Hunter:</b> Hunters are exceptional individuals, but still all to human. As such they would be no more or less attractive a target or have any inherent defenses. A possible exception might be the Lucifuge - a Xenomorph grown strong on demon tainted blood might exhibit otherworldly powers.<br /> <br /> <b>Sin Eaters: </b>A Sin Eater subjected to the gestation process would fare as well as a typical person, but with the bonus of being able to come back from the trauma. As far as the Xenomorph, the creature would likely gain the ability to perceive and interact with Ghosts, and could travel into the underworld through Avernan Gates.<br /> <br /> <b>Mummy: </b>Much like Vampires, Mummies are True Undead, and would likely be ignored by a protomorph. Even on the off chance that they get implanted, the empryo would be unlikely to make it to term - The Rite of Return would not allow such an indignity to befall one of the Arisen.<br /> <br /> <b>Demon: </b>As part of their Cover, a Demon appears human for all intents and purposes. This would leave them vulnerable to the attention of a Protomorph. However, by switching to a different Cover sidesteps the issue, the xenomorph embryo disappearing with the Cover. The same applies if the Demon Goes Loud. If the Xenomorph is allowed to fully develop,it would be considered a Cryptid, and would likely have a few appropriate crypitid abilities.<br /> <br /> <b>Beast: </b>A Xenomorph that gestates within a beast would become the worst thing a Best could imagine - a Hero. As such, it would be drawn to slay Beasts on an instinctive level, and could slip into the Primordial Dream, allowing it invade Lairs. Surviving a xenomorph embryo would depend on the Beast, some are unearthly tough, and could shrug off the trauma, others would be as dead as any mortal. Strangely, Beast might consider Xenomorphs &quot;Kin&quot; , and try to &quot;train&quot; them to serve.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T13:50:50-07:00","id":1085572,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar775_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"775\" data-vbnamecard=\"775\">Reighnhell</a> huh, nice work as usual!<br /> <br /> The Hunter part got me thinking again, for there are other, definetely physically changed Hunters that work for someone that gives of <b>very</b> strong Weyland-Yutani vibes: The Cheiron Corp.!<br /> I'd say a sufficiently enough changed employee would pass on some of his implanted abilities (possibly the implants themselves, depending on what they are?), which could range from simply being able to perceive Ghosts to feeling when e.g. Kindred are around etc., and I am convinced Cheiron would be more than willing to make a few sacrifices to procure some Xenomorph specimens FOR SCIENCE!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T13:59:53-07:00","id":1085575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1083939-effects-of-xenomorph-impregnation-oh-various-splats?p=1085572#post1085572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar775_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"775\" data-vbnamecard=\"775\">Reighnhell</a> huh, nice work as usual!<br /> <br /> The Hunter part got me thinking again, for there are other, definetely physically changed Hunters that work for someone that gives of <b>very</b> strong Weyland-Yutani vibes: The Cheiron Corp.!<br /> I'd say a sufficiently enough changed employee would pass on some of his implanted abilities (possibly the implants themselves, depending on what they are?), which could range from simply being able to perceive Ghosts to feeling when e.g. Kindred are around etc., and I am convinced Cheiron would be more than willing to make a few sacrifices to procure some Xenomorph specimens FOR SCIENCE!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Maybe Cheiron could replace Weyland-Yutani in a Xenomorph situation in the Infinite Macabre shard","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T14:51:41-07:00","id":1085596,"title":"","content":"You know, as they take on the traits of their predecessors... It's very possible that a Xenomorph who came from a mage might actually be innately more aware than other xenomorphs. Perhaps it seems to have no other effect besides a normal mortal, but it does take something more than purely biological traits -- namely, the human capacity to Awaken - or it comes out with the ability to affect supernal phenomena (if you want to break things less)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T17:53:47-07:00","id":1085633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div cla