r Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T14:22:43-07:00","id":1087337,"title":"","content":"Leviathan: The leviathan's biology would detect the foreign implant and assimilate it, resulting in a Lahmasu xenomorph that's the biological child of the Leviathan. With the right Adaptation a Leviathan could easily purge the egg from their body.<br /> <br /> Among Leviathans it is considered low-brow to implant your own chest bursting eggs into xenomorphs for bragging rights.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T15:37:05-07:00","id":1087362,"title":"","content":"I remember reading the books when they <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">get loose on Earth. They start implanting in the various animals they can find. There was a lot to do with cows, since they're so docile and numerous once you find them, but some had taken over large dogs, resulting in smaller ones, and I recall mention of a facehugger attached to a shark, though we never saw the result.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T10:51:50-07:00","id":1088383,"title":"","content":"Ok, so the more I think about it the more I think. for literary purposes, Changeling would have the scariest of all aliens. <br /> <br /> I'm looking at it from the perspective of giving an excuse to create scary and horrifying antagonists for a game. so regardless of possibility of gestation, I'm just handwaving it and assuming that a Facehugger did catch one and the resultant Xenomorph is different for each. <br /> <br /> So I'll look at each one in brief but I don't know much about a few of the splats so really I'm stretching this whole concept pretty far so that I can get an interesting amount of variation. <br /> <br /> <b>Vampire:</b> This one is not that interesting comparatively as I agree the result would be similar to a ghoul but all the same I think it would be interesting if it inherited certain abilities like protean that would make it distinct from the others. <br /> <br /> <b>Werewolf:</b> Handwaving out how survivable it would be for the Werewolf in question, the most interesting result would be a half-spirit Xenomorph with a Gauru-line form, ridiculous healing abilities, and Uratha-like abilities relating to the Hunt. In essence, the resulting Xenomorph would be a spiritual plague/infestation. I think what would be most interesting is if more than One Alien occurred due to this. the Queen -&gt; drone social structure would be very very different and a hive of Werewolf bred Xenomorphs would make for a most interesting Forsaken story line. Master-hunters hunting bastard half-spirit master-hunter infestations.<br /> <br /> <b>Mage:</b> This one you have to handwave quite a bit but it is near essential in order to create a unique antagonist creature. So, What if, the gestation rode the link the Mage's soul has to the Supernal (aka, just a /shrug lets make it work for the sake of the story kinda thing). Essentially the developing Xenomorph gets seeped in Abyssal-stuff. The resulting Xenomorph wouldn't make meaningful magic per-say but things would happen around it that correspond to it's desires. Creepy and corrupting things. Essentially make it like you would an abyssal entity. <br /> <br /> <b>Promethean:</b> So this one would be interesting. Something that caters to the themes of both Xenomorphs and Prometheans. I like this as kind of a reverse Promethean journey and a long-term antagonist. So first imagine that the flame infuses with the Xenomorph and simultaneously does not fully nourish it at the same time. It would take multiple times to complete the Xenomorph into adulthood. So after the first impregnation, the Xenomorph would need to infuse itself with a Promethean's flame with each time growing more and getting stronger. Not sure what the end result would be but I kinda like the idea of the end result being... a Promethean... thing... like not really promethean... but something... The idea hear is to keep the idea of ever changing and transmutations. <br /> <br /> <b>Changelings:</b> Now this is the one I wanted to talk about because as I thought about it it would be horrifying. Obviously you have to hand wave some things and make assumptions but the biggest one I like is that Xenomorphs inherit less of the seemings/kiths (though would be cool if it got some qualities based on it's host and environment but that's just fluff) and more straight up connections to the Wyrd. The most important of these would be the Mask. And it would be a bit of an enhanced version of the Mask. Essentially its mask looks human or like a dog or something and the Xenomorph would move to make that consistent. The reason this is horrifying to me is the idea of a silent person walking slowly to you while just under the surface it's this thing that wants to eat you and/or provide more hosts for facehuggers. Think of the movie <i>It Follows</i> for why this image is terrifying. And the deception would be thematic for Changeling games. <br /> <br /> <b>Hunter:</b> This one could be one of two things and both are interesting to me. First option is to make it the typical Xenormorph. It would be perfectly acceptable for Hunters vs Aliens and would be within the theme. The other option is to inherit the Vigil or what the Slashers have. Something that makes it either more vicious and inhumane or one that is attracted to other monsters (meaning you either exterminate it or let it lead you to other monsters at the risk that more Xenomorphs with varying forms start to spring up). Either is interesting for a Hunter game.<br /> <br /> <b>Sin-Eaters:</b> I kinda like the idea that the Geist transfers over to the Xenomorph and the Sineater host legit dies. This ramps up the horror for sin-eaters attempting to combat it as well as neccessitating trying to figure out who the Geist is/was. Additionally that would allow for ghost-like phenomena to occur around the Xenomorph (notably interesting is Boneyard effects) that would be the Geist doing things around the Xenomorph host. Additionally that would be interesting for the Xenomorph to act sometimes a little odd as the geist gets some of it's wishes. An unpredictable Xenomorph as it were. <br /> <br /> <b>Mummy:</b> Ok, I know basically nothing about Mummies. I'm sure I could create something that would be scary and thematic but I've really no idea. <br /> <br /> <b>Demon:</b> So this could go one of two ways and both kind of interesting though I like the latter of the two. The first option is to have it be a regular Xenomorph but it transfers from Cover to Cover so it's more likely to be born and the result would basically be a regular Xenomorph with a glitch or two and one or more Cryptid traits. The other option is for it to become something like a Fractal. Since the horror of the host dying as a result, it could be that the resulting Xenomorph becomes a Fractal and canabalizes the meta-physical body of the Demon's true form and inherets some bastardized forms abilities that the Demon possessed. It would also likely have Glitches and a few Cryptid abilities. I like this idea because it's more terrifying for Demons dealing with it. <br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> So I don't know much about Beast to be honest. But what if the physical form of the Xenomorph never really gets any bigger and could stay small inside the host. Instead it would grow out of the Beasts Horror and go rampaging that way. Essentially it replaces the horror and is a true parasite. Can't kill one without the other.<br /> <br /> <b>Deviant:</b> We don't know much yet, but so far? Highly unstable Chronenburg Xenomorphs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T10:11:09-07:00","id":1088789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1083939-effects-of-xenomorph-impregnation-oh-various-splats?p=1087362#post1087362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember reading the books</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC in one of the old Aliens game modules a Xeno egg falls into the water on an aquatic alien world <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">and is swallowed by a <i>megalodon</i>. The result is basically a small, maneuverable submarine made of gruesome, tearing death.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T10:30:55-07:00","id":1088793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1083939-effects-of-xenomorph-impregnation-oh-various-splats?p=1084241#post1084241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I, for one, would dread running into a xenomorph that popped out of a Deviant...<br /> <br /> Also, I'd go the other way around - xenomorphs that pop out of a werewolf are based off whatever form they were in at the time (it integrates itself into your system, you see). No, the problem is that the chestburster doesn't <i>kill</i> the werewolf. So theoretically, you could have a single werewolf become a chestburster <i>factory</i>...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The facehugger essentially hits you with a retrovirus that hijacks your body and reprograms it to grow a xenomorph, incorporating bits of the host's DNA into it as well.<br /> <br /> The SCARY part isn't the chestburster that comes out, while werewolves DO have some slight differences in DNA, who knows how much that will enable the resulting xenomorph to use the Shadow.<br /> <br /> The scary part is that the host, if it survives the chestburster, has xenomorph DNA in them and it has been shown in the books/comics/4th movie that the DNA starts to change the host. Madness, acidic blood, access to the hive mind, and so on are all things that can happen as the xenomorph DNA continues to integrate itself into the host long after the host should've been dead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8762-waywardpaladin","name":"WaywardPaladin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T10:32:53-07:00","id":1088795,"title":"","content":"All that being said, Lucifuge Xenomorph. A Xenomorph that can summon hellfire, incorporate demon traits into its body, command spirits and the like....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8762-waywardpaladin","name":"WaywardPaladin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T12:16:40-07:00","id":1100915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1083939-effects-of-xenomorph-impregnation-oh-various-splats?p=1084855#post1084855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love this idea. I might use something like this in a future Werewolf game.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was the premise of our original San Francisco Territory Werewolf Game 5-6 years ago or so... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Was a ton of fun. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}